.TH BIGINTMULFFT 3 "2026-09-21" "BigNums" "Library Functions Manual"
.nr HY 0
.ds AD l
.SH NAME
bigIntMulFFT \- multiply two big integers using FFT convolution
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include \(dqbignums.h\(dq
.sp
.BI "int bigIntMulFFT(BigInt *" "result" ", const BigInt *" "a" ","
.BI "    const BigInt *" "b" ");"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Multiplies a by b and stores the product in result.
The destination may be the same object as either or both inputs.
The inputs must be initialized; a distinct destination need not be.
.PP
Each 32-bit limb is split into two base-65536 digits.  The implementation
uses a power-of-two FFT convolution, rounds coefficients, propagates carries,
and repacks the limbs.  Temporary heap buffers are freed before return.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns 0 on success, INT_MAX if the product exceeds MAX_LIMBS, or \-1 on
allocation or FFT failure.  No caller-side deallocation is required.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR bigIntMulUInt_32 (3),
.BR fft (3),
.BR bignums (3),
.BR bignums (7)
